<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Waltrude</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 688</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Saint Waudru</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Waltrude was a Frankish noblewoman who founded a religious community at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> in Hainaut in the seventh century, around which the town grew. Married to Vincent Madelgarius and the mother of children also venerated as saints, she withdrew to a life of prayer. She is the patron saint of Mons, and her relics are carried through the town each year in the Car d'Or procession.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-waltrude.jpg" alt="Saint Waltrude" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jmh2o · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soignies_-_buste_de_sainte_Waudru_-_bois_polychrom%C3%A9_et_dor%C3%A9_-_1691-1710_-_2025-09-28_-_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
